/E (The part of the design process that is in dependent of any specific hardware or software platform is referred to as logical design. During logical design, all functional features of the system chosen for development in the analysis phase are described independently of any computer platform. Logical design concentrates on the business aspects of the system and tends to be oriented to a high level of specificity. During the logical design of the proposed system, all the functional features of the system which are identified during the analysis phase are collected and properly specified independent of any hardware and software specifications. )
/Pg 43 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
