1689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 503 0 R
/E (provides a structured representation of process flows, ensuring clarity and better comprehension for both technical and non-technical stakeholders. It contributes to effective project documentation, supports system validation, and facilitates future modifications and improvements. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [8 9]
>>
endobj
1690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 503 0 R
/E (The purpose of an activity diagram is to visually represent the workflow or behavior of a system, showing the sequence of activities and the flow of control or data between them. It is used to model business processes, system operations, and functional workflows, making it easier to understand how different tasks are executed within a system. By providing a clear representation of the process logic, it helps in analyzing, designing, and improving system functionality. Activity diagrams play a crucial role in requirement analysis by identifying functional requirements and ensuring that all process flows are well-defined before implementation. They help developers and stakeholders understand how a system operates by depicting various execution paths, decision-making points, and interactions between different activities. This makes them useful for designing algorithms, workflows, and system processes. In software development, activity diagrams facilitate the design of efficient workflows by illustrating both sequential and parallel processing. By incorporating decision nodes, forks, and joins, they help in managing complex execution flows and multi-threaded processes. They also assist in identifying potential bottlenecks, improving system efficiency, and ensuring smooth execution of tasks. Beyond software design, activity diagrams serve as effective documentation tools, enhancing communication among developers, business analysts, and stakeholders. They provide a structured overview of system processes, making it easier to maintain, scale, and modify workflows as needed. Additionally, they support system testing by helping to identify test cases and potential failure points, ensuring a more reliable and optimized software solution. )
/Pg 69 0 R
/K [10 11]
>>
endobj
1691 0 obj
<<
